Begin with the states prepared by a $z$-oriented apparatus: $\begin{aligned}
\ket{u}&\longleftrightarrow \sigma_z=+1,\\
\ket{d}&\longleftrightarrow \sigma_z=-1.\end{aligned}$ The letters $u,d$, the signs $+,-$, and the arrows $\uparrow,\downarrow$ are alternative labels for the same two preparations. Since a $z$-measurement distinguishes them with certainty, their state vectors are orthogonal: $\braket{u}{d}=0.$ Choose them to have unit length, $\braket{u}{u}=\braket{d}{d}=1.$

