p.src:
The overall minus sign of $\ket{l}$ is conventional. Replacing $\ket{l}$ by $-\ket{l}$ changes none of its probabilities. Adding and subtracting Equations  and  gives the inverse change of basis: $\begin{aligned}
\ket{u}&=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}\bigl(\ket{r}+\ket{l}\bigr),\\
\ket{d}&=\frac{1}{\sqrt2}\bigl(\ket{r}-\ket{l}\bigr).\end{aligned}$ The symmetry is important. Starting from the $x$-basis, an up or down state is an equal-weight superposition of right and left, just as a right or left state is an equal-weight superposition of up and down.

